I had been having some annoying luck trying to get through a caveman on
my normal account, so I decided to make another account to play some
more fun roles for a while. This game started out as a conduct monk
attempt. This initially changed on dlvl2, where I found an armor shop,
and "For you, most gracious lady; only 18000 for this long sword named
Frost Brand." I run back to dlvl1 and grab my kitten to steal it out of
the shop, and manage to id some boots that I had found earlier as speed
boots. At this point, it is T:1161.

I ditch the pet again (pets are irritating when you are very fast) and
continue down. I ignore the delicatessen on dlvl3, and move onto dlvl4.
I find a wand in one of the rooms and engrave test it... You may wish
for an object.--More-- (T:1444). I quickly wish up two scrolls of
charging, and was about to wish up the Eye when I realized that at
xlvl3, I only had 21hp... that wouldn't have gone well. I grab a "oRef,
and save the rest of the wishes for after I level up a bit.

I decide to stick with the main dungeon for a while, finding another
armor shop at dlvl7. At this point I realize that I have over 40hp, so
I wish up the Eye, the Orb (man do I love that thing), and a +ID. The
shop turns out to have a HoB and jumping boots, saving me another
couple wishes.

At this point (T:2535), I decide that I'm strong enough to get to
minetown (mine's end is unnecessary with the Orb), so I eyeport back to
the mines, and dive to minetown. The hardware store has a magic lamp,
and a BoH, which means I can skip soko also. Izchak's only has one
candle, but it also has a magic lamp, so I don't have much to complain
about there.

I eyeport back to the main dungeon and continue diving. Around T:3000,
anselmus convinces me to switch to the jumping boots and go for a speed
ascension, so at this point, the #jumping commences. I grab the food
from the first soko level to be able to keep this up, and this is where
I make my first major mistake - I jump around in soko out of habit
without really thinking, taking my luck down to -2, meaning no #pray
and no wishing until i fix it. Luckily, there was a cross-aligned altar
right outside, and the first soko level had a /CM, so I went back there
to fix that issue, and ended up with a gift of Giantslayer, which was
great, since it unrestricted long swords and made Frost Brand actually
usable. At this point I levport down to dlvl12, since dlvl11 is the big
room, and looked pretty dangerous.

My last wish is +MagicMissile, since I seriously needed a ranged
attack, and I figured anything else I really needed could wait until
the castle. I hit dlvl13, which has a wand shop, and get "You see here
a wand of wishing." (T:4006). This basically makes a speed ascension
mandatory, so I quickly wish up a /Death to take care of the shk (I
figure my luck can take it, after the sacrificing I had been doing, and
I didn't have telepathy). The shk drops a /Striking, which was quite
relieving, since up until this point I had no way of getting into the
castle. I then quickly wish up some other essentials that would take
too long to find normally - an athame, a unihorn, and ?Geno (L and ;)
and continue downward.

Dlvl14 brings a general store, which gives me =SD, /Poly,
+MagicMapping, and another magic lamp. I eyeport back to soko with this
loot (along with a bunch of raw scrolls and potions) and make a stash
there. By dlvl17 (T:4487), I decide that holy water would be a good
idea, since there was a fountain right by the upstair, so I eyeport
back to soko and grab my potions. I take the one !Water that I had
found over to the altar and prayed for holy water, then levport back to
pickaxe the fountain and go swimming for a bit. The holy water lets me
finally read +MagicMapping and +RemoveCurse. The level also has a
barracks, which I clear out for more rations.

Titan Medusa is at dlvl21, so I levport down to 22 to avoid dealing
with it, and jump my way to the castle at dlvl25. The moat has some
gremlins sitting in it, so I decide it's finally time for a marker
wish, and g goes away. I then use the /Striking to knock down the
drawbridge (T:4997), and take out most of the castle with magic missile
from across the moat. I also wish up =Conf about halfway through to
speed up the process, using the last non-wrest wish from my two wands.
I grab more food from the barracks, leaving the storeroom food for the
way up, grab a /Death from the fire giant in the throne room, and sit
on the throne. "You sit on the opulent throne.  You may wish for an
object.--More--" (T:5206). I grab a =Lev with that, and pick up a set
of black dragon scales also, since I already have reflection, MR, and a
marker.

I enter the valley at T:5271 with the intention of clearing it out for
scrolls and potions (which I have been quite short of up until now),
and to get some wraith corpses, since I am still xlvl12 at this point.
All the wraith corpses I get turn out to be rotten, but I do get a
decent supply of scrolls, potions, and spellbooks, as well as a
/Cancel. I buy protection once from the priest there (for 4ac), and
then eyeport back to soko.

Now (T:5619) I figure it's finally time to do some polypiling to fill
in the rest of the things I would like to have. I end up with
+HasteSelf (which lets me wear jumping permanently), +DrainLife (which
I had been considering wishing up for Kaen), +EH (nice, since I only
had 67hp at the time), and a few extra copies of some useful wands. I
then enchant up my armor and weapon, and then wish up a cursed magic
marker for some revgeno action. I get teleportitis from a leprechaun,
and three levels from two groups of wraiths. I also write up another
blessed geno to take out h, which finishes off all of the dangerous
monsters.

My next goal is the quest. I leave soko and levport to the quest level
(T:6021) and find the quest at T:6036. I'm quite nervous about Kaen at
this point, only having 71hp, so I wish up a "LS, and make all kinds of
preparations at the downstair to Kaen's lair, so that I can just
teleport to the stairs, go up, and read a ?Earth as quickly as
possible. Unfortunately, I go to wake him up, only to see "Master Kaen
drinks a murky potion!--More-- Master Kaen rises up, through the
ceiling!". This worries me, since I need to be on the upstair in order
to finish this quickly, but I know I can't last long if he starts
attacking. I end up levporting up two levels to come down the stairs
from above. Kaen is in the room, so i read a ?Earth immediately, but he
doesn't move. I sigh, write up another scroll of earth, zap striking at
the boulders on the stair, and move to zap Kaen to wake him up, when he
starts attacking. The first round of hits brings me from 71hp to 39hp,
which makes me very grateful for that +EH. I back off, and he follows
me, hitting me again, but giving me a chance to teleport back to the
stairs and read the ?Earth. After this, it is pretty trivial with +DL,
and I finish him off and eyeport back to the valley.

I reach Gehennom at T:6252, levport to the bottom, and find the VS by
T:6302 (man am I getting lucky this game). I then levport up to the
lowest possible level for Vlad's entrance, and work my way up from
there, finally finding Vlad at Orcustown (T:6472). I pick up the "LS,
kill Vlad, and then get another "You sit on the opulent throne.  You
may wish for an object." I grabbed =FA here, since at this point I'm
seriously running out of things to wish for, and made my way back down.
On my way out, I realize that it has been quite a while since my last
prayer, so I pray for food, since rations are starting to get a little
tight.

Next, I levport back to the level right above the VS, to start working
my way up to find the tower; luckily (seeing a pattern here yet?) the
portal is on that level. I enter Rodney's tower at T:6677, and levport
up two levels to get to the top. I had picked up a c corpse on my way
there, and I intended to hit him with it to save some /Death charges,
but neglected to take into account the severe effect wearing armor
would have on my hit chances, causing another close call - he stole the
Eyes, forcing me to have to beat him to death with Frost Brand (still
at 71hp). After that scare, I decide that going without dsm is the
better option, since AC isn't quite as important with the Orb, so I
take off the suit, wish up 7 candles and levport back to the VS, and
finally "You are standing at the top of a stairwell leading down!" at
T:6809.

The high priest is another battle I'm not looking forward to at this
point, so I alchemize up some !FH. I only get 4, but 103hp is a pretty
significant improvement at this point, especially since I have +EH. I
also write up some more ?EA to improve my AC without the DSM to -11 (it
had been -22 with it). I finally levport into the sanctum, but can't
manage to land on the left. Stealth gets me through the graveyard,
however, and the rest of the sanctum is pretty much a breeze with
conflict. /Death on the high priest, and I finally get the Amulet
(T:6922). I also finally picked up a /Tele, which I had also been
planning on wishing up at some point in the near future. I burn a magic
lamp for a c!GL to get out of the sanctum, and start the climb up at
T:6927.

At first, it looks like it's going great - the VS is on dlvl46, and I
don't hit the force at all up through dlvl39. I write up some charging
here to get pw back so I can keep the mapping and teleporting up, and
finally reach the tower levels. I get up through Orcustown, when the
force finally starts hitting, and hitting hard. I had to go through 9
unnecessary notele levels at this point, which used up almost all of
the food I had with me. I figured I still had enough to make it back to
the castle storeroom at this point, so I kept going on. Baal and Asmo
were paid off easily, and their levels weren't a problem. I took
Juiblex across the swamp, and made it up to dlvl28 with no force
problems - it looked like I was going to make it. The force had other
ideas though - i redid 6 dlvls29-27, bringing me back up to the valley
weak, with no food and no /Tele charges, since I had used them as a
source of hungerless tele.I knew I couldn't make it back across the
valley like this, so I was forced to burn another wish on c!GL. This
got me back to the castle storeroom easily enough, and I started the
run up through the main dungeon with 9 food rations at T:7740.

The run up here was pretty uneventful - ran past the titan at Medusa,
and did mapping + teleport for the rest of the way up, jumping and
writing up ?MM when I ran out of pw. I made it to the upstair at dlvl1
at T:7952. I alchemized up the rest of the potions I had collected to
bring my hp up to 142, and wrote up a couple more ?Charging, and
entered the planes at T:7979.

The planes were pretty straightforward - locate the portal with the
Orb, and conflict took care of the rest. I got to Air at T:8031, Fire
at T:8076, Water at T:8118, and Astral at T:8186. I realized I had
still never gotten telepathy, so I just picked a direction and went
with it - ended up jumping right by Death and landing on the neutral
altar at T:8203, just 17 turns after entering Astral.

